(a) A license issued hereunder shall stand automatically revoked without further action by the City of Moultrie:
(1) Whenever the state shall revoke or fail to renew any permit or license to manufacture or sell at wholesale or retail any alcoholic beverages, the city license to manufacture or sell at wholesale or retail any such product within the city shall thereupon be automatically and immediately revoked without any further action by the mayor and council or any officer of the city. If the state has suspended the license or placed the same on probation, the city license is automatically suspended or probated, as the case may be.
(2) Whenever a license holder fails pay any penalty set forth in subsection 6-199(a) within ten days of its imposition the license issued by the city shall be automatically revoked without any further action by the mayor and council or any officer of the city.
(3) Whenever a licensee fails to have a valid state license, either by suspension, revocation, nonrenewal or expiration, the license issued by the city shall be automatically revoked without any further action by the mayor and council or any officer of the city.
(4) Revocations pursuant to this section become immediately effective upon the happening of the event triggering revocation and there shall be no further sales, consumption, or storage of any alcoholic beverages by the prior licensee or on the previously licensed premises.
(b) All rights and privileges conveyed by a license issued by the city shall terminate upon the first to occur of the following:
(1) Death of the licensee, except to the extent on any right to continue to utilize such license as provided in subsection 6-102(b);
(2) Dissolution of a corporation or partnership which are holder of such license;
(3) The filing of any voluntary bankruptcy proceedings under the bankruptcy code by the licensee or the failure of the licensee to, within 60 days of the date of filing thereof, obtain dismissal of the involuntary proceeding filed under the bankruptcy code against the licensee;
(4) Lapse of such license pursuant to the provisions of this article;
(5) Denial by the city manager of an application for renewal of such license;
(6) Revocation thereof by the city manager;
(7) Surrender of license;
(8) Automatically without any action on the part of the city upon revocation by the Georgia Department of Revenue of any alcoholic beverage license issued by the Georgia Department of Revenue to the licensee in issue with respect to such location; or
(9) The licensee ceases to be engaged in the sale of alcoholic beverages permitted by such license pursuant to section 6-38(b).
Any licensee whose license is revoked or terminated pursuant to this section shall not thereafter resume the sale of any alcoholic beverages at any time until they have complied with the requirements this chapter and made application to the city manager, such application by the licensee or at the same location shall be treated as a new application.
(Ord. No. 771, § 1(4-72), 12-16-1997; Ord. No. 970-2006, § 1, 1-3-2006; Ord. No. 2020-222, § 1, 3-17-2020; Ord. No. 2020-241, § 13, 11-17-2020)
Editor's note— Ord. No. 2020-241, § 13, adopted Nov. 17, 2020 amended § 6-163 and in doing so changed the title of said section from "Automatic revocation" to "Automatic revocation; termination," as set out herein.

